	"notes": [
		{
			"id": "n45sHZILMHMgDt5LG",
			"text": "Typical Stats from the package record: ST 20, DX 11, IQ 4, HT 11, HP 22, WILL 10, PER 4, FP 11, SPEED 5.5, MOVE 5, DODGE 8, DR 0. GCS derives its own values by applying the ancestry; where the two differ, the package's Typical Stats are what the Dungeons on Automatic encounter tables use."
		},
		{
			"id": "nGjjjydqDyihilm73",
			"text": "Encounter rating: CER 31 (offense 8, protection 23), threat tier standard, appearing 2."
		},
		{
			"id": "n3oTyzcXN3VKTPdIu",
			"text": "GCS ancestry draft: gcs/warhorse-skeleton.gct"
		},
		{
			"id": "nJjSfLdvmHyoSIce0",
			"text": "Independent build total: 224 points of racial traits plus 1 points of racial skills."
		},
		{
			"id": "n5SWEUqEGOkse_x4_",
			"text": "Answers the SRD heading(s): Warhorse Skeleton (SRD 5.1). Only the creature identity is taken from the SRD; the GURPS statistics, ratings and prose are this project's own work and reproduce no SRD text."
		},
		{
			"id": "nFvJbgQWlSm7amfuB",
			"text": "Typical Stats, damage and ratings are derived from the racial template, not authored beside it, so the sheet and the stat block cannot disagree."
		},
		{
			"id": "n9z-GS1wJrIRdx0XW",
			"text": "Body mass used to scale this build: 60 kg. ST, Size Modifier and DR are checked against it; see the gurps-animal-sanity-check skill for the bands."
		},
		{
			"id": "nEI0LrmrEsS9Z1xEn",
			"text": "Movement: ground Move 5, 10 at a sprint (primary). The published Move is the primary medium's cruising Move; sprint figures are stated here and not folded into it."
		},
		{
			"id": "nM1oqTvc8cHDeZwBg",
			"text": "Treasure and grappling are not authored for this batch and ship as explicit nulls; `lair` carries a short habitat note, because where a wandering animal dens is an encounter fact rather than a loot one."
		},
		{
			"id": "no0Fdh9zCW0hB13aj",
			"text": "Still a two-hex quadruped; the ground speed of the living animal is kept with a level of Enhanced Move."
		},
		{
			"id": "n0juP-XDneLz1VSLn",
			"text": "It accepts any rider and no rider; a skeleton mount is tack, not a companion animal."
		},
		{
			"id": "n-WmHNoi-O9QKyqyi",
			"text": "Monster statistics, ratings and description prose by Monsters on Automatic; AI-generated first draft, project-reviewed, released under CC BY 4.0."
